WEBVTT

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.460
This is a spooky house.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.700
Who's there?

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:09.740
We're sorry. We had no idea anyone lived here.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.840
We're just keeping out of the rain too.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:17.850
What are...

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.910
They're specimens of giant salamanders.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.090
What was in this place?

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:36.390
Probably some kind of bio-research facility, I guess.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.430
What's more, these are clones.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.170
They could do things like that in the old days.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:51.370
Kiyoko!

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:12.420
What's wrong?

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:15.870
I couldn't sleep.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.040
This spot is calming somehow, isn't it?

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.970
Yeah, it's not bad, I guess.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.680
Hey, Tatsuya...

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.590
Why did you suddenly come to visit my apartment?

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.250
Well...

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.390
Was there something you needed?

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.400
Well, I wouldn't go that far,

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.670
...but I got to wanting to hear about Dad again.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.430
It was only that?

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.000
Yeah, that's all right, isn't it?

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:04.450
I don't remember anything but what I told you before.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:06.780
Oh...

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:11.580
It's weird somehow, this wanting to hear about Dad stuff.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.920
You're the one who's getting to look exactly like him.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.420
It's like you ought to just ask yourself about him.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.500
Come here.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:40.410
We used to sleep resting our shoulders together like this, didn't we?

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.710
Yeah...

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:45.920
I like your body; it's so warm.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.390
And your cheeks are soft too.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.950
Cut it out, will you?

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:57.190
Come to think of it, Dad's body was warm too.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.030
Even though Mom's wasn't.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.640
What's the matter, that brings you to a place like this?

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:10.570
It's... Well, it's just cozier under here.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.380
We're sorry.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.890
You need not apologize.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:21.990
Providing our guests the most pleasant spaces possible is our motto.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:27.660
If you say you are more able to relax here, please use this space as you like.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.130
All right...

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.470
Thank you.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:32.530
Let's give it a try...

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.130
If I may disturb you for a moment...

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.250
Oh, I see. It is nice.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.550
Now that I think of it, I recall that when I was a boy,

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:53.010
...when I went inside the closet, it put me into a strangely calm mood.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.020
Perhaps it's what you'd call a longing to return to the womb.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.090
I'm sorry for telling such a boring story.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.060
I shall bring you some blankets.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:38.790
Who's there?!

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:45.640
Just now, I could have killed you, Mr. Kazamatsuri.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.640
A Peeping Tom, eh? That's not a nice hobby.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.280
You just happened to be doing that when I came in, that's all.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:57.520
Walking in openly through the front door would be lacking in flair, wouldn't it?

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.560
You're not alone, correct?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:05.130
The sight was a bit too provocative for them.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:09.800
And? What is it you want?

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:16.140
The one who told Madoka that he's Enkidu's clone was you, right, Mr. Kazamatsuri?

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.940
That's right.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.840
Mr. Kazamatsuri, you said this before...

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.780
"About Orga and about Dynamis..."

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.240
"If that's the case, then shall I tell you?"

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:30.880
Ah, and so you've come to ask me.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:35.750
Won't you tell us about ourselves, as you did with Madoka?

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.430
There are equally big secrets about us, aren't there?

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.260
You ought to ask the Countess.

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:45.200
If it were you, Mr. Kazamatsuri, could you ask her?

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:48.770
True enough.

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:57.680
Very well, I'll tell all of you about Dynamis, and about Orga-Superior.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:19.190
With that, I've said all that I'm able to say.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.070
Is that all you want to ask?

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.270
Let's go home.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:34.880
I think I'll ask that you go out this way.

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.400
Oh, by the way...

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:49.360
I believe I'll pay a visit to the Hotel Providence in the near future,

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:51.730
...so I trust you'll treat me favorably.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:06.380
Only the killing of Gilgamesh affirms the Blattaria's existence, you see.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:08.890
Did they go home?

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:09.880
Yeah...

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.590
There's something creepy about those kids.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:20.250
It's like, they really aren't like normal people, huh?

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:23.700
That goes for that girl Kiyoko too though.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:24.870
Oh?

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:27.700
It was my job, so I stuck close to her even though I didn't want to,

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.100
...but that kind of girl makes my skin crawl.

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:36.100
Making a face like, "I'm carrying the whole world's misfortune on my back all alone."

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:41.050
Gloomy, I guess you'd call her. She even made me feel miserable.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:47.260
That girl isn't, by any chance, the same breed as those kids from just now?

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:49.120
If so, then she really is unfortunate.

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:52.160
They're not proper human beings after all.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.830
I'm surprised they can stand to be alive and not kill themselves.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:17.850
What'd you do that for? What was that for, all of a sudden?!

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.230
Where have you been?

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:06.440
Just over to Kazamatsuri's for a bit.

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:07.500
Huh?!

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:11.970
We asked him to tell us about ourselves too, and not just you.

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.040
So, we heard his answer...

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:30.320
Very well, I'll tell all of you about Dynamis, and about Orga-Superior.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:39.000
You know about Heaven's Gate in a general way, don't you?

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:41.000
Yes...

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:46.910
All of the experiments performed there carried great dangers.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:53.410
Nobody's survival could be guaranteed in the case of an accident occurring.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.550
But that was the age when science was all-powerful.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:04.690
At Heaven's Gate, they had preserved cloned embryos of the scientists in advance, as backups.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:13.770
The institution that maintained those scientists' cloned embryos was Orga.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:17.770
At a certain point,

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:24.440
...it was identified that an unknown life form had been born inside Delphys.

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:31.120
Since the lot number was T-e-Ar, the life form was called "Tear."

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:33.820
Tear?

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:39.830
The results of an investigation proved that the peculiar light emitted by Tear...

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:45.530
...was penetrating through all the special protective plating and contaminating the whole of Heaven's Gate.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:51.800
The executives decided to seal off Delphys and close Heaven's Gate.

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:56.280
I don't know the details, but it was because it became certain,

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:59.550
...that if things were left as they were, it would bring about the downfall of the human race.

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:04.450
A few days later, the XX incident occurred.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:18.370
Heaven's Gate was ruined, and every nation or corporation involved...

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:23.530
organized an investigative committee and rushed to clear away the negative legacy.

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:33.080
In the midst of that confusion, a variety of assets flowed onto the black market.

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:40.850
Among those, the ones traded at the highest prices were the cloned embryos from Orga.

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:50.200
That's because most of the Heaven's Gate scientists were designer children, with combinations of superior genes.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:55.640
But even the cloned embryos of Orga, which were supposed to have been kept under strict safekeeping,

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:57.840
...had been contaminated by the light from Tear.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:04.540
That fact was identified after the children had actually been born.

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:14.750
Those children uniformly possessed a special power called Dynamis.

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:19.760
They came to be called "Orga-Superior."

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:31.240
Perhaps this is more than I should say, but...

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:37.240
This is our opportunity, so can't you tell us?

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:42.480
It's about the cloned embryos that went onto the market...

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:46.520
Probably the lucky ones were born of women,

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.590
...but most of them...

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.800
With that, I've said all that I'm able to say.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.570
Is that all you want to ask?

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:13.010
So we're clones, just like you, Madoka, of somebody from Heaven's Gate.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:19.060
Just because you've got the technology to create something,

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.250
...doesn't mean you should create it so hastily and lightly.

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:25.720
For us, who were born that way, it's unbearable.

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:30.970
Madoka, you're still better off than us, because at least your mother gave birth to you.

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:37.010
It could be that we were...

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:58.290
Tatsuya?

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:25.020
Kiyoko!

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:43.670
Get down!

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:55.910
You're in our way!

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.460
Kiyoko!

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:13.660
Tatsuya!

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:21.270
Kiyoko...

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:46.430
Kiyoko?

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:00.450
What's this?

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.600
What's that?

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:16.060
Dynamis?

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.700
Call the doctor for me.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:58.840
This is the second time we've met here, isn't it?

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:03.240
My worries that time proved to be right on the mark.

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:08.210
The awakening of Dynamis within you stems from the child you are carrying.

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:15.060
I don't know what occurred that led to this state of affairs, and I don't want to know,

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:19.090
...but it is at the stage a human fetus would reach at three months.

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:21.100
It is indeed a beast.

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:27.470
The object of Blattaria's raid was that child.

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:31.900
If that's so, there's no need to go so far as to enlist their help.

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:38.300
The arrangements for the surgery will be finished momentarily.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:41.250
It's all right with you, of course?

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:42.590
No, it's not.

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:43.850
No?

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:47.010
No, this is my child.

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:50.950
I didn't think you were that foolish.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:55.100
Perhaps you take after your mother.

00:20:55.100 --> 00:21:00.060
But I'm not so lenient as to permit such stupidity.

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:08.710
The thing you're carrying is a monster, do you hear me?

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:14.510
The instant it raises its first cry, who knows what sort of misfortune it will bring upon the world.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:19.620
Show a little intelligence and listen to what I'm saying.

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:25.680
Or will you run away? Just as you did that other time?

00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:27.950
You know, isn't it about time you had a mind of your own?

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:29.790
Instead of just going along with whatever anyone tells you?

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:32.360
Yeah, but it's been nothing but unbearable stuff!

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:34.960
That guy has no emotions...

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:38.030
Both the stuff about us and this stuff with Kiyoko.

00:23:38.030 --> 00:23:39.000
...what's wrong with using Dynamis?

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.930
I'm exhausted somehow.

00:23:41.670 --> 00:23:43.220
Hey, give me a little?

00:23:43.830 --> 00:23:45.460
I feel like I'll get a nosebleed.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:47.570
Nothing special.

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:48.560
Just a little!

00:23:51.440 --> 00:23:52.640
Just a little...

00:23:53.380 --> 00:23:54.280
Okay?
